WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.204
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.204 --> 00:00:12.883
Today, publishing: the card people see, drafts and versions,

5
00:00:12.883 --> 00:00:16.378
and how to update a world without upsetting your players.

6
00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.108
Click Publish up top.

7
00:00:19.108 --> 00:00:24.028
The cover image goes on your world's card and its page, and Save and publish,

8
00:00:24.028 --> 00:00:27.670
right beside it, is the button that puts your draft live.

9
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.308
World name is the title players see.

10
00:00:30.308 --> 00:00:35.503
The card description is the short pitch on the card, two hundred and sixty characters,

11
00:00:35.503 --> 00:00:39.430
and it's used on the page too if you leave the description empty.

12
00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:44.873
The description is the long one on your world's page, and it takes formatting.

13
00:00:44.873 --> 00:00:48.853
Ours says what the show is, what you get, and how it was made.

14
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:55.312
Links to Voyage, Discord, Latitude and AI Dungeon are the only ones people can click,

15
00:00:55.312 --> 00:00:57.787
so put anything else as plain text.

16
00:00:58.233 --> 00:01:01.555
And tags, up to ten, help people find it.

17
00:01:01.555 --> 00:01:05.931
Ours: circus, road trip, comedy, fantasy and tutorial.

18
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:12.867
Scroll on down past the Studio notes, which are private and players never see,

19
00:01:12.867 --> 00:01:16.202
and type says whether this is a world or a mod.

20
00:01:16.202 --> 00:01:17.550
Ours stays a world.

21
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.168
Visibility is for your draft: private is only you, unlisted is anyone with the link.

22
00:01:23.168 --> 00:01:27.044
It doesn't touch the published version until you publish again.

23
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:33.303
Allow remix publishing says whether players can publish their own remixes of your world.

24
00:01:33.303 --> 00:01:35.546
They can always make private ones.

25
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.439
And the content rating check suggests the rating players will see.

26
00:01:40.439 --> 00:01:44.139
Run it again after big changes, and before you publish.

27
00:01:45.533 --> 00:01:48.275
Once it's live, every update is a new version.

28
00:01:48.275 --> 00:01:54.057
Games already going keep playing the version they started on, so only new games get your changes.

29
00:01:54.057 --> 00:01:59.361
And on your world's page, the Updates tab lets you post news without publishing anything.

30
00:01:59.361 --> 00:02:02.461
I post mine silent so nobody gets pinged every time.

31
00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:05.216
That's publishing.

32
00:02:05.216 --> 00:02:08.064
Our card is linked in the description.

33
00:02:08.064 --> 00:02:13.909
Next time, settings, and the Creator API that lets you skip Studio altogether.

34
00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:18.315
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

